Ladybird represents a hole in dictionary storage by an absent
index. V8’s DictionaryElementsAccessor::GetEntryForIndexImpl()
looks up the key in a NumberDictionary. JavaScriptCore’s
JSObject::getOwnPropertySlotByIndex() checks indexed storage and its
sparse map. SpiderMonkey’s NativeLookupOwnPropertyInline() checks dense
elements and the shape’s property map.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 reported the same
own keys and lengths before and after concatenating sparse arrays of
lengths 3, 64, and 256. An explicit undefined kept its own index.
